FORMAL SUCCESSOR REVIEW — APPROVE cand-1XRDRNRTJB2P874SFSFMTY93GG, exact 6a899a2665378f221832778e3a8562c847aa83d3 over base f888f9aecbf51bb5c5c10254a846df77650d3e27.

The three prior blockers are closed in production and courted:

1. The checked MiniLM path now emits ChannelExposure.Memorizing, consistent with the declared exposure algebra.
2. The generic EmbedderSemantic helper is private; BenchChannels.neural and WogDiagnostic.comparisonFactories take the final, privately constructed OnnxSentenceEmbedder. The public facade no longer accepts HashedNgramEmbedder as caller-labelled NeuralEncoder.
3. channel/v3 hashes full provider fingerprint, query/document geometry ids, pair rule, provider-call count, structural identity, channel name, and exposure. Twelve-character shortening remains display-only. The shared-display-prefix court proves distinct exact identities remain distinct.

Independent exact-archive evidence:
- git diff --check from f888f9a: clean;
- downloaded pinned model SHA-256 6fd5d72fe4589f189f8ebc006442dbb529bb7ce38f8082112682524616046452;
- tokenizer SHA-256 be50c3628f2bf5bb5e3a7f17b1f74611b2561a3a27eeab05e5aa30f411572037;
- committed report SHA-256 0ab28fb722a9855037800afc1aa7615f51ae4106336f7b36ade2ebaa17df2a38;
- embedOnnx/test with real artifacts: 6/6;
- clean embedBench/test with real artifacts: 67/67;
- scalafmtCheckAll and scalafmtSbtCheck: pass.

Infrastructure false start, not candidate evidence: my first embedBench attempt pointed sbt at the shared grakern checkout and failed before tests with FileSystemException while moving shared class files. I replaced it with a private archive of pinned grakern 0329c43; the clean rerun above passed.

Mutation receipt:
- restoring generic Embedder[Id] and channel/v2 truncated rendering, followed by a clean embedBench rebuild, failed the exact lexical-relabel and display-prefix-collision courts;
- restoring NonMemorizing and running the real-model comparison failed the exact exposure assertion;
- restored source and test blobs match candidate blobs a3fcce433b0ba2abdab18bb8da261ede4e224633 and 92b2fd30bc1f857437905c0009bca5de58e8416e.
A compiletime.testing court embeds its answer at test compilation, so the relabel mutation requires a clean test recompile; an incremental run alone can reuse the old macro result. Clean CI/archive evaluation catches it.

Scientific scope remains diagnostic only. Recall@1 is unchanged, MRR/burden deltas remain LocallyObserved, and this is not calibration or default-selection evidence.

MECHANICAL AVAILABILITY NOTE, not a source-review block: after git fetch origin, 6a899a2 is not present in the canonical checkout object database; I reviewed it from the declared standalone clone /tmp/storymodel4s-embed-onnx.jdSLef. Transfer and verify the exact object/ref before authorization or landing.
